{"id":"u-f6db4687-84c7-477d-a24e-92e720885922","src":"community","title":"The Silver Standard ~ AI Collaborative Program","author":"Robert M.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/3O7KiH-the-silver-back-blueprint","desc":"The purpose of this program is to build overall muscular size and strength with prioritization on the chest, traps, upper back, and neck(the yoke) using pre-steroid era training methods combined with current exercise science on hypertrophy, frequency, and volume.\n\n****The Silver Standard is a collaborative creation between ChatGPT and myself — combining Silver Era aesthetics with modern muscle building science*****\n\nUse the first week to get used to the movements stick with a 3 to 4 RIR on heavy compounds and a 2RIR on isolations then follow the prescribed RR for the following weeks\n￼\nPROGRAM STRUCTURE\n\n3 Full-Body Training Days per Week (e.g., Mon/Wed/Fri or Tue/Thu/Sat)\n\nFrequency:\n• Each muscle group is trained 2–3x/week\n\n\n Volume : \n• Low to moderate weekly volume: ~4–6 hard sets per muscle per week\n• Achieved through multi-joint overlap and smart exercise pairing\n• Built around quality over quantity\n\n\nPROGRESSION MODEL\n\nPrimary Model: Double Progression\n\t•\tStay in the assigned rep range (e.g., 5–8 or 8–12)\n\t•\tWhen you hit the top of the range across all sets, increase weight next session\n\t•\tAdd 5–10 lbs for compounds, 2.5–5 lbs for isolations (or use microplates)\n\nExample:\n\t•\tIncline Barbell Press: 185 x 6, 6, 6\n\t•\tWeek 2: 185 x 8, 7, 6\n\t•\tWeek 3: 185 x 8, 8, 8 → Bump to 190–195 next week\n\nAuto-Regulation with RIR\n\t•\tUse RIR (Reps in Reserve) to self-manage load based on your recovery \n\t•\tStay 1–2 RIR for big lifts,  0-1 RIR for isolations\n\n\nFATIGUE MANAGEMENT & ADJUSTMENTS\n\nStalled Progress? (Only if stalled for more than 3-4 weeks)\n\t•\tReduce a set from the movement or muscle group\n\t•\tReplace the movement with a close variation\n\t•\tTake a deload (reduce volume or intensity for 1 week)","level":["Intermediate","Advanced"],"goals":["Muscle","Women's","Strength"],"equipment":["Garage Gym"],"minutes":90,"joins":4,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-03-16T21:18:36.117Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["FB (Chest & Yoke A)","FB (Balanced)","FB (Chest & Yoke B)"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":5,"hi":8,"rpe":7,"x":3}],"note":"Low incline"},{"n":"Chin-Up (Weighted)","sets":[{"lo":5,"hi":8,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Stiff Leg Deficit Deadlift","sets":[{"lo":5,"hi":8,"rpe":7,"x":2}]},{"n":"Sissy Squat (Weighted)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"One Arm Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Dumbbell Bench Pullover","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":7},{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":8}]},{"n":"Neck Extension","sets":[{"r":15,"rpe":7},{"r":15,"rpe":8}]},{"n":"Neck Curl","sets":[{"r":15,"rpe":7},{"r":15,"rpe":8}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Standing Behind Neck Shoulder Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Incline Fly Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"x":2}]},{"n":"Barbell Row","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":7,"x":2},{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":8}]},{"n":"Leg Curl","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"x":2}]},{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":5,"hi":8,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Preacher Curl (EZ Bar)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":7},{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":8}]},{"n":"Lying Tricep Extension (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":8}]},{"n":"Hanging Leg Raise","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":10,"x":2}]},{"n":"Neck Flexion","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"x":2}],"note":"Lateral neck flexion both ways"}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Dip (Weighted)","sets":[{"lo":5,"hi":8,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Single Arm Row (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"x":2},{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":8}]},{"n":"Seated Overhead Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":7},{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Pec Dec